🚽 Test case: #196 -- by-value struct brace-init of a pointer-typed FIELD
🚽 (`gang Holder { gang Point *pt; }; gang Holder h = {&r};`) is checked
🚽 against the field's declared type/tag, the same as a plain field
🚽 assignment (`h.pt = &r;`, already checked) -- PR #248 review, round 5,
🚽 finding 1. This is a FIFTH place a pointer-to-struct value gets stored,
🚽 distinct from struct_init_expr/data.op.right/plain-assignment/array-
🚽 element-brace-init (rounds 1-4): the NODE_STRUCT_DEF arm of a
🚽 declaration's pending_initializer only ever propagated a contextual
🚽 type hint into each leaf (for slorp() resolution), never compared an
🚽 already-typed leaf like `&r` against the field it initializes.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Rect {
    rizz w;
    rizz h;
};
gang Holder {
    gang Point *pt;
};

skibidi bump(gang Point *pp) {
    yapping("%d %d", pp.x, pp.y);
}

skibidi main {
    gang Rect r;
    r.w = 11;
    r.h = 22;
    gang Holder h = { &r };
    bump(h.pt);
}
